# Deterministic line endings so raw-byte hashes (source_sha256, lock and record SHA-256 values) reproduce on any
# checkout regardless of core.autocrlf. Source, text and config files are pinned to LF, which is what produced the
# recorded hashes.
*.py    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
*.lock  text eol=lf
*.pt    binary

# Frozen, SHA-256-pinned files are kept as exact bytes (no end-of-line conversion, ever). The continuity fixtures
# were frozen on Windows with CRLF, and their recorded hashes are over those bytes.
tests/fixtures/*.json     -text
evidence/**               -text
# The pre-training seal was written on Windows with CRLF, and the checkpoint lock records the SHA-256 of those bytes
# (seal_sha256 91203089...). Kept as the exact original bytes (Amendment A7, owner decision 2026-10-11).
docs/PHYS-GEN-V1-SEAL.json -text
